WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.234
Laurie and Amy spent every day together, both of them enjoying the companionship of an old friend and familiar conversation.

2
00:00:08.235 --> 00:00:15.067
However, Amy sensed that Laurie was holding something back, and she had a good idea it had to do with Jo.

3
00:00:15.068 --> 00:00:21.528
One afternoon, while the two friends were relaxing—Amy sketching a paradise-like scene of fruit trees and birds

4
00:00:21.529 --> 00:00:26.015
while Laurie flipped through a bookㅡshe decided to ask Laurie about it.

5
00:00:26.016 --> 00:00:29.767
"Laurie?" Amy called in her most ladylike voice.

6
00:00:29.768 --> 00:00:33.258
"Did something happen between you and Jo?"

7
00:00:33.259 --> 00:00:36.733
Shutting his book, Laurie said, "What makes you ask?"

8
00:00:36.734 --> 00:00:42.061
Carefully choosing her words, Amy replied, "You used to be best friends,

9
00:00:42.062 --> 00:00:48.742
but I’ve noticed that whenever I mention her name or talk about something to do with Jo,

10
00:00:48.743 --> 00:00:52.880
you either change the subject or avoid the topic altogether."

11
00:00:52.881 --> 00:00:57.039
Laurie looked out at the scenery Amy was sketching and said nothing at first.

12
00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:00.485
Then, he said quietly, "She broke my heart, Amy."

13
00:01:00.486 --> 00:01:04.941
Setting aside her sketchbook, Amy walked over and sat next to him.

14
00:01:04.942 --> 00:01:09.185
"Sometimes talking about it can help," she said kindly.

15
00:01:09.186 --> 00:01:15.879
So Laurie began to tell her everything that happened, and Amy listened sympathetically.

16
00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:20.731
Back home, Jo knew from Amy’s letter that she had run into Laurie in Italy.

17
00:01:20.732 --> 00:01:25.209
But Jo did not have a clue the two of them were talking about her at that moment.

18
00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:30.125
Her thoughts were otherwise occupied as she worked frantically, her fingers numb and stiff,

19
00:01:30.126 --> 00:01:33.549
putting the finishing touches on the last paragraph of her story.

20
00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:39.813
Satisfied with the ending, Jo threw on her coat and headed toward the office of the Volcano magazine.

21
00:01:39.814 --> 00:01:46.067
The Volcano printed trashy stories, but Jo knew that’s what sold and she needed the money.

22
00:01:46.068 --> 00:01:51.743
Upon returning from the Volcano , Jo put her recent earnings into the box she had been saving her money

23
00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:56.143
in. It was almost full. She emptied the box and began

24
00:01:56.144 --> 00:02:00.731
counting. "Three hundred and fifty-two dollars and twenty cents," she

25
00:02:00.732 --> 00:02:02.962
calculated. "That should be enough for our

26
00:02:02.963 --> 00:02:09.042
trip." Suddenly feeling as though a large weight was lifted off her shoulders, Jo threw her coat back

27
00:02:09.043 --> 00:02:12.865
on. This time, she headed toward the coach office in

28
00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:19.056
town. After his intimate conversation with Amy, Laurie also felt as though a burden was lifted from his

29
00:02:19.057 --> 00:02:25.039
heart. He still thought of Jo, but not as often, and he noticed that he had begun to enjoy life

30
00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:31.905
again. Laurie had already been in Europe for over two months but only then did he feel as though his vacation was

31
00:02:31.906 --> 00:02:37.177
beginning. Amy was touched that Laurie had opened up and shared his heartbreaking experience with

32
00:02:37.178 --> 00:02:42.119
her. She knew–everyone did–that Laurie had had a crush on Jo for many years. She

33
00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:49.853
also knew that it was one-sided, and Jo never looked at Laurie as anything more than her best friend and a brother figure. "Miss

34
00:02:49.854 --> 00:02:54.969
Amy? Mr. Laurence is here," the servant announced through Amy’s door. "Thank

35
00:02:54.970 --> 00:03:03.338
you. Tell Mr. Laurence I’ll be right down," Amy called back, grinning at the thought of someone calling Laurie "Mr. Laurence." Tonight

36
00:03:03.339 --> 00:03:09.051
Laurie was taking Amy to the opera, so she had made an extra effort to look her best. Laurie

37
00:03:09.052 --> 00:03:15.014
seemed to notice how beautiful Amy looked, because upon seeing her walking down the stairs, he remarked, "I’m

38
00:03:15.015 --> 00:03:18.681
going to need a stick to keep all the young men away from you." Suddenly

39
00:03:18.682 --> 00:03:23.586
feeling shy, Amy blushed as she took his outstretched hand. Beth

40
00:03:23.587 --> 00:03:29.667
and Jo were not looking as lovely as Amy, but they were having a fantastic time as

41
00:03:29.668 --> 00:03:35.172
they poked their heads out of the coach to catch sight of endless rows of cornfields in Kansas.

42
00:03:35.173 --> 00:03:41.983
Their journey to California had begun three days ago, and it would take another week to arrive at their destination.

43
00:03:41.984 --> 00:03:50.380
The girls, however, were enjoying every moment as they saw new scenery, met interesting people, and heard a variety of accents along the way.

44
00:03:50.381 --> 00:03:54.488
"It’s a shame neither of us can draw like Amy," Jo kept saying,

45
00:03:54.489 --> 00:04:00.889
because she wanted somehow to preserve the memorable sights to remind herself of this trip in the future.

46
00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:04.975
However, Beth’s reply made it clear why she was taking this trip.

47
00:04:04.976 --> 00:04:10.757
"If we spent our time concentrating on one sight, we might miss out on the others.

48
00:04:10.758 --> 00:04:15.917
I’d rather see everything once than see the same scene over and over again.

49
00:04:15.918 --> 00:04:25.652
Besides, the picture we take with our heart is always so much more precious than the ones we capture with a brush, don’t you think?"

50
00:04:25.653 --> 00:04:32.611
Closing their eyes as the wind blew against their faces, Jo and Beth breathed the Midwestern air in deeply.

51
00:04:32.612 --> 00:04:36.671
Back home, Meg and Mother sat having tea and knitting clothes for the baby.

52
00:04:36.672 --> 00:04:41.938
Meg’s stomach was big, bigger than Mother’s had been during each of her pregnancies.

53
00:04:41.939 --> 00:04:49.041
"Meg, I don’t mean to alarm you, but has Dr. Bangs mentioned anything about your baby?" Mother said.

54
00:04:49.042 --> 00:04:53.171
"Why? Do you think there is something wrong?" Meg asked worriedly.

55
00:04:53.172 --> 00:05:02.891
"Dr. Bangs is much more knowledgeable in these matters, but I wouldn’t be surprised if you were carrying more than one," Mother said with a smile.

56
00:05:02.892 --> 00:05:05.669
Meg dropped her knitting and stared openmouthed.

57
00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:09.421
"You mean twins? I might be carrying twins?"

58
00:05:09.422 --> 00:05:17.807
Shrugging her shoulders, Mother replied, "It’s not so unusual, Meg, and you seem quite large to be having just one baby."

59
00:05:17.808 --> 00:05:24.155
Rubbing her big belly, Meg repeated disbelievingly, "There might be two babies inside?"

60
00:05:24.156 --> 00:05:27.999
Not realizing that she might become an aunt to two babies at once,

61
00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:35.597
Amy, after enjoying several evenings of dancing and partying, was becoming increasingly irritated at Laurie’s playboy approach to life.

62
00:05:35.598 --> 00:05:40.287
They sat in the sitting room of the villa Aunt March had rented having a serious chat.

63
00:05:40.288 --> 00:05:43.440
"When are you returning home?" she asked.

64
00:05:43.441 --> 00:05:46.727
"I haven’t really thought about it," he answered, shrugging.

65
00:05:46.728 --> 00:05:51.653
"What about graduation? What about finding a job?" she continued.

66
00:05:51.654 --> 00:05:58.408
"I don’t have to work, really. Grandfather can provide me with all that I need," Laurie replied as if he didn’t care.

67
00:05:58.409 --> 00:06:05.383
Amy, who was also knitting (all the March girls enjoyed it as a hobby), began clicking her needles faster and kept her mouth shut.

68
00:06:05.384 --> 00:06:10.085
"Are you upset about something?" Laurie asked, noticing Amy’s coldness.

69
00:06:10.086 --> 00:06:15.973
"Yes," she replied curtly. "You are the laziest boy I’ve ever met."

70
00:06:15.974 --> 00:06:19.936
Startled, Laurie asked her why she thought that.

71
00:06:19.937 --> 00:06:26.142
Putting her knitting down, Amy said, "Just because you’re rich doesn’t mean you should waste your life away.

72
00:06:26.143 --> 00:06:30.291
There is so much more for someone clever like you to do in this world.

73
00:06:30.292 --> 00:06:33.285
Money isn’t everything, Theodore Laurence!"

74
00:06:33.286 --> 00:06:39.886
With those words, Laurie, but more so Amy, was shocked to discover how much she had changed in the last year.

75
00:06:39.887 --> 00:06:45.881
"Why, Amy March, I never thought I’d hear you say that," Laurie said nastily.

76
00:06:45.882 --> 00:06:53.614
"Well, that’s how I feel, and shame on you for exploiting and wasting your grandfather’s money this way," Amy snapped at him.

77
00:06:53.615 --> 00:06:58.412
Standing up, Laurie said, "I can and will do as I choose."

78
00:06:58.413 --> 00:07:01.778
"Then do it," Amy said in a shaky voice.

79
00:07:01.779 --> 00:07:05.461
"But don’t do it around me, because I won’t stand for it."

80
00:07:05.462 --> 00:07:13.735
Grabbing his coat and hat, Laurie said coolly, "Take care, Amy. It was lovely to spend time with you, but I’m afraid the fun is over."

81
00:07:13.736 --> 00:07:17.233
And he walked out the door.

